(3,'🟡',"Insecure output handling and data exfiltration: how do model outputs become XSS, SQL or command injection, or leak data via markdown images and links, and what controls stop it (encode and sanitise, allowlist URLs, strip or proxy images, structured outputs, no auto-execution)? ",f"all types; security-aware GenAI roles; {O} lists improper output handling (LLM05)"),
# ---- 2 star ----
(2,'🟡',"Token, cost and latency accounting per request: how do you record input, output, cached and reasoning tokens, convert them to cost with versioned price tables, attribute cost to tenant, feature and prompt version, and reconcile with the provider invoice? (Part 10 Q13 covers self-hosted cost per token.)",f"product companies, GCCs, GenAI startups; Langfuse and Helicone docs describe usage and cost tracking; {G}"),
(2,'🟡',"What does an LLM gateway do (one API, key management, routing, fallbacks, retries with backoff, rate limits, caching, budgets, logging, guardrail hooks), what are the risks of adding one (latency, single point of failure, becoming a data honeypot), and build vs buy? (Part 10 Q28 covers routing and caching for cost.)",f"product companies, GCCs, platform teams; Helicone's docs describe fallbacks and rate limits; {G}"),
(2,'🟡',"Reliability patterns for calling LLM providers: timeouts, retries with jitter, 429 and retry-after, idempotency, circuit breakers, multi-provider fallback (and what breaks when the fallback model behaves differently), and graceful degradation.",f"product companies, platform teams; {G}"),
(2,'🟡',"Cost governance for a multi-tenant LLM product: per-tenant and per-user budgets, token-bucket quotas, soft vs hard limits, alerts before spend spikes, showback and chargeback, and denial-of-wallet protection. (Part 10 Q49 covers serving-side fairness.)",f"product companies, SaaS teams, GCCs; {O} describes denial of wallet under unbounded consumption (LLM10)"),
(2,'🟡',"Model and version pinning: why 'latest' aliases are dangerous, how do you handle provider deprecations and silent updates (pin dated snapshots, canary evals, regression suite, migration runbook, contract terms)? (Part 9 Q43 covers detection; this covers change management.)",f"product companies, GCCs; {G}"),
