(2,'🟡',"System prompt leakage and canary tokens: why you should assume the system prompt can be extracted, what must never be in it (secrets, credentials, authorisation logic), and how canary strings in prompts or documents help detect leaks and indirect injection exfiltration.",f"security-aware GenAI roles; {O} lists system prompt leakage (LLM07); {G}"),
(2,'🟡',"Excessive agency: how do you scope tools (read vs write, per-user credentials, allowlisted actions, spend and rate caps), when is human approval required, and how do you audit what an agent did? (Part 8 Q28 covers MCP threats; Part 8 Q50 enterprise MCP.)",f"security-aware GenAI roles, agent teams; {O} lists excessive agency (LLM06)"),
(2,'🟡',"Data and model poisoning, RAG corpus poisoning and supply chain: how can attackers affect fine-tuning data, adapters, embedding stores, shared prompts, model files and packages, and what controls apply (provenance, signed artefacts, safe formats, scanning, pinned dependencies, review of ingested content)?",f"security-aware GenAI roles, platform teams; {O} lists supply chain (LLM03) and data and model poisoning (LLM04)"),
(2,'🟡',"Multi-tenant isolation in RAG and caches: how do you enforce ACL-aware retrieval, per-tenant indexes vs filters, cache keys that include tenant and permission scope, and tests that prove no cross-tenant leakage? (Part 6 Q15 and Q42 cover access control basics; go to operations and testing.)",f"product companies, SaaS teams, GCCs; {O} lists vector and embedding weaknesses (LLM08); {G}"),
(2,'🟡',"How do you evaluate guardrails in production: false-positive cost (blocked legitimate users), detection latency, per-category precision and recall on a labelled and adversarial set, shadow mode before enforcing, and drift as attackers adapt? (Part 5 Q29 has the metrics; focus on rollout and monitoring.)",f"security-aware GenAI roles, product companies; {G}"),
(2,'🟡',"Red-teaming an LLM app in practice: scope and threat model, manual vs automated attack suites, tools and datasets, severity and exploitability triage, regression tests for fixed findings, and release gates. (Part 5 Q23 and Part 9 Q29 cover the basics.)",f"security-aware GenAI roles, product companies; {G}"),
(2,'🟡',"Secrets and key management in LLM apps: provider API keys, per-tenant keys, rotation, scoping and spend caps, why keys must not be in prompts, logs, client code or tool outputs, and how an agent should get credentials. ",f"product companies, platform teams; {G}"),
(2,'🟡',"Compliance and governance at a general level: audit logging, NIST AI RMF (Govern, Map, Measure, Manage) and its Generative AI Profile, the EU AI Act's risk-based approach, India's DPDP Act themes (consent, purpose limitation, data principal rights), and what an engineer should document. State clearly what you would defer to legal counsel.",f"GCCs, regulated-industry teams, enterprise roles; NIST page opened; EU and India legal details were not verified from primary text; {G}"),
(2,'🟡',"Model extraction and abuse: how do attackers copy model behaviour through queries, what do you limit (rate, logprobs, output volume), how do you detect scraping and abuse patterns, and what does watermarking or terms enforcement realistically achieve?",f"AI product companies, API providers; {O} describes model extraction under unbounded consumption (LLM10)"),
